tools/compare_matmul_paths.py after the XLA-verification fix, trn1.2xlarge,
2026-09-13. Run exactly as the README tells a reader to:
python tools/compare_matmul_paths.py (8192^3 bf16, 25 s each, one process).

The fix: the XLA half used to call its product "exact" from one element of the
warm-up pass, and threw the timed loop's product away. It now reads the timed
loop's last product back whole after the clock stops and checks every element
against K. The synced tool below is the patched one (md5 a8bb2609, and its
product_elements_wrong definition present).

    remote tool md5 a8bb2609
    === synced tool carries the fix: 1 (expect 1)
    === python tools/compare_matmul_paths.py (started 13:01:25)
    ....
