    exit 0 (finished 13:07:43)

What the run shows:

  - Both halves exact under the new standard. For XLA, exact True now means
    every one of the 8192^2 elements of the timed product equals 8192 -- not
    one corner of the warm-up.
  - XLA torch.matmul 66.20 TFLOPS, against 66.25 and 66.32 recorded on
    2026-09-10. Reading the whole product back after the timed loop did not
    move the timed figure.
  - NKI tensor_virus 78.03 TFLOPS, row-tiles checked. XLA is 0.85x the kernel:
    no meaningful gap by the tool's 1.2x band, the NKI kernel ahead -- the
    coalesced tiling's result, as the tool's docstring records.

The instance launched with instance-initiated shutdown set to terminate and a
shutdown timer armed, and was terminated directly once the run finished.
